vert $D$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -8 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(\\frac{2}{7}){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $D$ has $5$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $5.$"] [17592186124885 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [17592186121910 :answer-field/correct 17592186121911]] "retractions" [[17592186124885 :question/problem "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $D$, given by\n$D = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -8 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$."]]}]